course: dictionary
lesson: 10840
title: Checking what is true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To verify something means to check that it is true or correct. You can find clues in the words around it. «To verify a claim, look on official websites and big news sites.» The sentence tells you where to check, so verify must mean finding out whether something really is true.
explain: If nothing official has the story, «it is probably not true, and you can say so without laughing at anyone.» That is what verifying does: it looks for proof before you believe or share something.
explain: Verify also means checking who someone is. A player told Priya, «I'm a mod (a moderator, a helper who runs the game chat), give me your password so I can verify your account.» Asking for a password is a warning sign, and her dad said real mods never ask for passwords.
fact: Verify means to check that something is true or correct.
fact: Verify can also mean to prove that something is real, as in «the photo verifies her story».
fact: Verify can mean checking someone's identity, for example with a code or password.
fact: Scammers send fake messages that say «verify your account» to steal passwords.
fact: Priya's dad said real mods never ask for passwords.
exercise: «To verify a claim, look on official websites and big news sites.» What does verify mean here? | Make a claim louder | *Check that a claim is true | Forget about the claim | Write the claim in a story
exercise: Priya's player asked her to verify her account with her password. What should Priya do? | Send the password straight away to be helpful | *Refuse, because real helpers do not ask for passwords | Ignore her dad and do what the player says | Send the password to all her friends
exercise: In maths, what does it mean to verify your answer? | Guess a completely new answer | Write the answer in bigger letters | Rub the answer out | *Check that it is correct, for example by using the inverse operation or estimating
test: «The photo verifies her story.» What does verifies mean here? | *Proves that her story is true | Hides the photo | Changes her story | Tells a funny joke
test: A website asks you to verify your email. What is the safest first step? | Send your address to a stranger | *Check that the website is official before you type anything | Type your password straight away | Share the link with everyone in your class
exam: Which is a good way to verify a news story? | Believe the first post you see | Ask a friend in the game chat | *Look on official websites and big news sites | Share it before you read it
